{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T11:11:26.285Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f76476df464406160904c840","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-07T11:11:26.285Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Strengthened the regression to exercise the actual detached launch path, replacing the earlier inline negative control. A Node preload observes telemetry-flush.js spawns through the public child_process API and delays actual flush-worker startup by 2 seconds. Removing only PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED launched a worker that survived the foreground init (476 ms); regression failed 0/1 on the explicit no-detached-workers assertion. Its teardown terminated observed worker PIDs and awaited their exit before removal, with no cleanup failure. Restoring the flag passed 1/1. Telemetry settings stay enabled, inherited opt-outs are cleared, test events are opted in, the endpoint is loopback, and OTEL delivery is disabled in the negative control. Initial npm gate passed 533/533 and 100/100/100; rerunning after this regression refinement."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T11:11:26.285Z"}],"before_hash":"f3b955a302f31db78fe352300cd4121a2d5cf7504d9e26ea07bb1b19194fdaf6","after_hash":"ed50e09b00c44b6495d6118c419fc20a4605068e81bf402426ee89fa4972cc50","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"recor